        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_82a5551e89604d8aaaa4f2c8a8c72c42",
      "statement": "The WebSocket onclose handler interprets close codes: 1000 does nothing; 1001 hands the close reason to reconnect(url, reason) as a migration redirect; 1006, 1011, 1012, and 1013 all feed the reconnect loop; any other code rejects the still-pending connect Promise and fires onZeroHubError.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L1319-L1368",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d36000e1e9fe52d95945f74e83e13d52ef3f579d85b29b1786d35c83bc092c4f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_94fcb528042c4c2e97fadddc7328073e",
      "statement": "connectToZeroHub resets isDisconnected to false, cancels any queued same-host retry timer, and clears the reconnectAbandoned latch, so a client that previously called disconnect() or hit a terminal error can start a clean reusable connection on any new entry point. Pending ICE candidate timeouts are intentionally NOT reset here.",
      "evidence": [
