    {
      "id": "claim_bd4128b0cd9d456c8ec9c4355a36c977",
      "statement": "SFUTopology routes all P2P traffic through a single SFU peer (lowest numeric peer ID by default, or an explicitly set one via parseInt(id,10) sort); the SFU offers to every client and non-SFU peers connect only to the SFU. When the currently elected SFU leaves the hub, reElectSfu re-elects the lowest remaining peer and re-establishes the star, deduped by lastElectingSfuId; an explicitly configured sfuPeerId is never overridden. On WebRTCDisconnected only the SFU side re-sends an offer.",
