    {
      "id": "claim_0bb2463bfe094c7db8b7ead9edcf6878",
      "statement": "Reconnect is bounded and not single-shot: every host gets maxReconnectAttempts same-host retries with exponential backoff, then the sweep fails over across configured hosts and wraps back to the first host, bounded by maxReconnectRounds full sweeps; only when every host's budget is spent on every allowed sweep does the client latch reconnectAbandoned and surface the terminal error 'all ZeroHub hosts are not working, please check the ZeroHub hosts' via onZeroHubError.",
      "evidence": [
