    {
      "id": "claim_2b6a3e2ef22b4cc387020205c3a3370c",
      "statement": "The WebSocket onerror handler logs and fires onZeroHubError but does not call reconnect: per RFC 6455 a network failure fires error and then close with code 1006, and reconnecting in both handlers would advance hostIndex twice for a single failure; all reconnection is handled in onclose. The error also settles the connect Promise to avoid a permanently pending promise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L1297-L1318",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce5a7b31b264dd7b690ec5642652225853c87b1d15c35ca8c5dea4895cbca36c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d7994bff5cc4ef1aa3bd7aaf510d9a3",
      "statement": "All four hub connection entrypoints (joinStaticHub, joinOrCreateIPHub, createRandomHub, joinRandomHub) funnel into the private openHubConnection helper, which stores supplied metadata, builds a URL from getWS(host, tls) with id/hubMetadata/peerMetadata query params, and calls connectToZeroHub. The former createHub/joinHub/joinOrCreateHub and createPermanentHub/joinPermanentHub entry points were removed; joinIPHub was also removed because a client-supplied id can never resolve to an IP hub.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L1812-L1881",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a7f6e0f1e317e31a232457f896fd2c4f9fb78b877a97856c7b61bfedf54e07f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_94dec8e87c65413b9d94fa60a17902c9",
      "statement": "On a hubInfoMessage the client reconciles its local peer roster against the authoritative roster carried in the message: it adds any roster peer not yet in the map and prunes any peer it still holds that is no longer listed and is not itself, firing ZeroHubDisconnected and tearing the peer down via removePeer. This prune pass is the auto-reconnect fix; without it a peer that left the hub while the socket was down would linger as a stale Peer with a live, unclosed RTCPeerConnection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L804-L839",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3d0b505365f1fcf569ad0e1ce62d17196b3cf4e497b4e748839f64e935777da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2fc909679c64c51b575825c7dc469b9",
      "statement": "Hub and peer metadata received from the server is parsed through the module-level safeParseJson(raw, fallback) helper, which returns the parsed JSON on success or the fallback when the input is missing or malformed; the caller logs a warning only on a genuine parse failure, so a corrupt metadata value from the server degrades to the fallback instead of throwing and crashing the WebSocket message dispatcher.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L1123-L1141",
