    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fe80df61090748b8992b0111552683e8",
      "statement": "On a 1001 migration redirect, reconnect first validates the close reason with isWellFormedHost (a bare hostname or host:port with no scheme, path, userinfo, whitespace, or port > 65535, mirroring the server's validateBackupHost); a malformed reason falls back to the automatic recovery path without touching host state, and a reason equal to the current host is rejected through onZeroHubError instead of retrying. On a valid redirect the client updates this.host and, when the target is in the configured hosts list, points hostIndex at its position.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/utils.ts#L51-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b42185d8f66f226f899c5e67177fc31146534146875516ff50408cabeb73f80a:"
