    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fab1320d27cb4ee9b13d4d8609736414",
      "statement": "connectToZeroHub tears down any live WebSocket through the shared private closeActiveSocket helper before creating the new socket: the previous socket's onclose/onerror/onmessage/onopen handlers are nulled (so it cannot fire reconnect() and advance hostIndex a second time, or a spurious onZeroHubError), then it is closed with code 1000 and this.ws is cleared. The same helper is used by disconnect().",
