        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea59de1b8139452d86d9932f2f146675",
      "statement": "With autoAnswer: false, the offerMessage branch does not call sendAnswer; it moves the peer to AnswerPending and invokes the public onOffer(peer, offerSdp) callback (guarded on the peer existing in the peers map) so the application completes the exchange via sendAnswer(peer.id, offerSdp). With autoAcceptAnswer: false, the answerMessage branch moves the peer to AcceptPending and invokes the public onAnswer(peer, answerSdp) callback so the application completes the exchange via acceptAnswer(peer.id, answerSdp). Both callbacks are isolated from throwing handlers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L840-L901",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7cdf88a6b09e213116646c15766262bd6acfddd2a0d6babbe7fc1841e4a5608c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_229a309d921a4176b3233d02a2dac5c5",
      "statement": "ZeroHubClient exposes two public callbacks for manual SDP handling: onOffer(peer, offerSdp) is invoked when an offerMessage arrives while autoAnswer is false (peer already in AnswerPending); onAnswer(peer, answerSdp) is invoked when an answerMessage arrives while autoAcceptAnswer is false (peer already in AcceptPending). Both callbacks are guarded on the peer still existing in this.peers, so a dangling offer/answer for a peer already torn down is not surfaced.",
      "evidence": [
